            <ArticleTitle>Orofacial Pain Overview: Getting Rid of the Riddles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>729-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While most pains that find their way to the dental office are dental in origin, some have less familiar roots: muscular, joint, neurological, headache, sinus or psychological. All of these roots can at times masquerade as a toothache. The purpose of this article is to alert the dentist to the select features of each root that distinguish it from the rest, resulting in efficient and appropriate treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
